<title>UK: Details of UK Jan car registrations' 7.8 pct rise.</title>
<headline>Details of UK Jan car registrations' 7.8 pct rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's SMMT Ltd auto trade body issued the following details of new car registrations for January showing how registrations rose by 7.8 percent.</p>
<p>JANUARY</p>
<p>Top 10 by marque, market share in pct vs year ago.</p>
<p> Ford	     40,451  (19.56 pct) vs  41,837  (21.82 pct)</p>
<p> GM-Vauxhall    30,274  (14.64 pct) vs  27,957  (14.58 pct)</p>
<p> Rover	    18,535   (8.96 pct) vs  20,776  (10.83 pct)</p>
<p> Renault	  15,074   (7.29 pct) vs  11,695   (6.10 pct)</p>
<p> Peugeot	  14,987   (7.25 pct) vs  14,708   (7.67 pct)</p>
<p> Citroen	  11,371   (5.50 pct) vs   9,808   (5.11 pct)</p>
<p> Volkswagen     10,558   (5.11 pct) vs   9,249   (4.82 pct)</p>
<p> Nissan	    8,930   (4.32 pct) vs   7,477   (3.90 pct)</p>
<p> Toyota	    6,736   (3.26 pct) vs   5,148   (2.68 pct)</p>
<p> Fiat		6,508   (3.15 pct) vs   6,868   (3.58 pct)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
